  "_README": [
    "Pro forma assumptions for Misty Valley Supply. Every number here is an",
    "ASSUMPTION until Ben replaces it with a real quote, a real invoice, or a",
    "real payroll number. The point of the model is not to predict -- it is to",
    "show which assumptions the business is actually sensitive to.",
    "",
    "Unit basis: one road-legal truckload = ~95,000 linear feet of stud and",
    "track at a blended 0.463 lb/ft across a representative commercial job mix,",
    "against a 44,000 lb road-legal dray limit. See container_model.py.",
    "",
    "Pricing basis: distributor-to-contractor of $0.70-0.95/LF triangulated in",
    "04-unit-economics.md, against verified Louisville retail of $1.268/LF",
    "(Home Depot ProSTUD 25, 3-5/8in x 10ft, checked 2026-09-04).",
    "",
    "Volume basis: 04-unit-economics.md sizes total corridor demand at 40-100",
    "loads/month and realistic new-entrant capture at 0.5-3/month in years 1-2.",
    "The base case ramps inside that range and does not assume otherwise."
